From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:48:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: let an i386 child's opengl32 attach with the GL-absent
 table

0068 gave an i386 child's unix libraries their WoW64 tables and every
other library the stub table, whose every code fails. opengl32's own
table on iOS is the GL-absent one, whose attach codes (process_attach,
thread_attach, process_detach) succeed; replaced by the stub table,
opengl32's DllMain failed with STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED, and so did every
i386 process that loads it: STATUS_DLL_INIT_FAILED (0xc0000142) before
the game's first line. That is any i386 title that imports opengl32 and
any that reaches wined3d, which imports it: Super Meat Boy's d3dx9_43
imports d3dcompiler_43, which imports wined3d.

The GL-absent table reads no parameter block, so it serves a WoW64
caller as it is. An i386 child now gets what a 64-bit process gets:
opengl32 loads and every GL and WGL call fails with
STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED, since there is no OpenGL on iOS. The [unixlib]
WoW64 line names the table "(GL-absent table)".

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-08-wow64-opengl32.md
Offered-upstream: no; the stub tables exist only on the iOS port
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index c64eeb6..5f4c488 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -7595,13 +7595,18 @@ static NTSTATUS load_builtin_unixlib( void *module, BOOL wow, const void **funcs
             else if (*funcs == (const void *)nsi_unix_call_funcs) wow_funcs = nsi_unix_call_wow64_funcs;
             else if (*funcs == (const void *)playport_steam_unix_call_funcs) wow_funcs = playport_steam_unix_call_funcs;
             else if (*funcs == (const void *)playport_url_unix_call_funcs) wow_funcs = playport_url_unix_call_funcs;
+            /* opengl32's GL-absent table reads no parameter block, so it serves an
+             * i386 child as it is: its attach codes succeed, so opengl32 (and
+             * wined3d, which imports it) loads, and every GL call fails */
+            else if (*funcs == (const void *)ios_gl_stub_unix_call_table) wow_funcs = ios_gl_stub_unix_call_table;
             if (!wow_funcs)
             {
                 pthread_once( &ios_stub_tables_once, ios_init_stub_tables );
                 wow_funcs = ios_stub_unix_call_table;
             }
             dprintf( 2, "[unixlib] module %p (%s) WoW64 -> %p%s\n", module, match ? match : "(null)",
-                     wow_funcs, wow_funcs == (const void *)ios_stub_unix_call_table ? " (stub table)" : "" );
+                     wow_funcs, wow_funcs == (const void *)ios_stub_unix_call_table ? " (stub table)" :
+                     wow_funcs == (const void *)ios_gl_stub_unix_call_table ? " (GL-absent table)" : "" );
             *funcs = wow_funcs;
         }
     }
